WEBVTT

00:02.258 --> 00:03.885
KATARA: Water.

00:04.844 --> 00:06.221
Earth.

00:06.804 --> 00:08.223
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:10.517
Air.

00:11.351 --> 00:14.604
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.271 --> 00:18.566
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.609 --> 00:22.570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.654 --> 00:23.863
could stop them.

00:23.947 --> 00:26.866
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.242 --> 00:28.368
A hundred years passed,

00:28.451 --> 00:30.870
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:30.954 --> 00:32.705
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.914 --> 00:35.041
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.124 --> 00:37.710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.794 --> 00:38.795
AANG: Oof.

00:38.878 --> 00:41.839
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:47.845 --> 00:50.056
ROKU: Previously on Avatar...

00:50.348 --> 00:53.643
KATARA: I can't believe we finally made it
to Ba Sing Se in one piece.

00:53.893 --> 00:59.774
I just want our new place to look nice,
in case someone brings home a lady friend.

00:59.857 --> 01:01.859
ZUKO: I don't want to make a life here.

01:02.068 --> 01:04.445
JOO DEE: Here we are,
your new home.

01:05.113 --> 01:07.073
We need to talk to the king
about the war.

01:07.156 --> 01:10.660
Your request for an audience
with the Earth King is being processed,

01:10.743 --> 01:12.787
and should be put through
in about a month!

01:13.162 --> 01:16.833
If we're gonna be here for a month,
we should spend our time looking for Appa.

01:36.728 --> 01:37.770
( CLICKING TONGUE )

01:41.482 --> 01:42.734
( CHIRPING )

01:45.612 --> 01:46.863
( GASPING )

01:46.946 --> 01:49.073
Toph, aren't you
gonna get ready for the day?

01:51.618 --> 01:52.702
( HOCKING AND SPITTING )

01:56.122 --> 01:57.206
I'm ready.

01:57.290 --> 01:58.833
You're not gonna wash up?

01:58.916 --> 02:02.253
You've got a little dirt on your...
Everywhere, actually.

02:02.670 --> 02:06.466
You call it dirt, I call it
a healthy coating of earth.

02:06.549 --> 02:07.675
Hmm...

02:07.759 --> 02:09.135
You know what we need?

02:09.469 --> 02:11.429
A girls' day out!

02:11.804 --> 02:13.264
Do I have to?

02:13.348 --> 02:14.891
KATARA: It'll be fun.

02:19.103 --> 02:21.189
TOPH: The Fancy Lady Day Spa?

02:21.272 --> 02:23.149
Sounds like my kind of place.

02:23.608 --> 02:25.902
Are you ready for
some serious pampering?

02:26.569 --> 02:28.237
( HESITATING ) Sure, Katara.

02:28.321 --> 02:29.781
Whatever you say.

02:29.864 --> 02:31.699
As long as
they don't touch my feet.

02:36.829 --> 02:37.830
( SCRAPING )

02:38.206 --> 02:40.166
( GRUNTING AND GROWLING )

02:41.668 --> 02:42.710
Ugh!

02:42.794 --> 02:43.795
Uh...

02:49.050 --> 02:50.968
( BLOWING )

02:52.053 --> 02:53.763
( SCREAMING )

02:54.347 --> 02:56.808
( BOTH LAUGHING )

03:03.064 --> 03:04.857
( BOTH SIGHING )

03:07.110 --> 03:08.820
Well, that wasn't so bad.

03:09.070 --> 03:13.449
I'm not usually into that stuff,
but I actually feel... Girly.

03:13.700 --> 03:14.742
KATARA: I'm glad.

03:14.826 --> 03:16.994
It's about time
we did something fun together.

03:22.333 --> 03:24.001
Wow, great makeup.

03:24.085 --> 03:25.086
Thanks.

03:25.253 --> 03:26.504
For a clown.

03:27.004 --> 03:29.382
( LAUGHING )

03:30.216 --> 03:32.385
Don't listen to them.
Let's just keep walking.

03:32.719 --> 03:34.512
I think she looks cute.

03:34.595 --> 03:37.473
Like that time we put a sweater
on your pet poodle-monkey.

03:37.557 --> 03:39.726
( LAUGHTER )

03:40.727 --> 03:41.936
GIRL: Good one, Star.

03:42.520 --> 03:43.896
Let's go, Toph.

03:44.021 --> 03:46.691
TOPH: No, no,
that was a good one.

03:46.774 --> 03:48.192
"Like your poodle-monkey."

03:48.276 --> 03:49.986
( LAUGHING )

03:50.069 --> 03:51.863
You, you know what else
is a good one?

03:53.114 --> 03:54.115
( SCREAMING )

03:56.159 --> 03:57.744
Now that was funny.

03:58.953 --> 04:00.204
( SCREAMING )

04:00.747 --> 04:03.082
Those girls don't know what
they're talking about.

04:03.374 --> 04:04.542
TOPH: It's okay.

04:04.625 --> 04:06.502
One of the good things
about being blind

04:06.586 --> 04:09.881
Is that I don't have to waste my time
worrying about appearances.

04:09.964 --> 04:11.841
I don't care what I look like.

04:11.924 --> 04:14.093
I'm not looking for
anyone's approval.

04:14.594 --> 04:16.220
I know who I am.

04:16.304 --> 04:18.765
KATARA: That's what
I really admire about you, Toph.

04:19.098 --> 04:21.768
You're so strong and confident
and self-assured.

04:22.059 --> 04:23.186
( SNIFFING )

04:23.269 --> 04:25.438
And I know
it doesn't matter, but...

04:25.688 --> 04:27.190
You're really pretty.

04:27.690 --> 04:28.733
I am?

04:29.025 --> 04:30.401
Yeah, you are.

04:34.906 --> 04:38.409
TOPH: I'd return the compliment,
but I have no idea what you look like.

04:38.493 --> 04:39.702
( KATARA LAUGHING )

04:39.786 --> 04:40.995
TOPH: Thank you, Katara.

04:41.078 --> 04:42.163
KATARA: Ow!

04:55.760 --> 04:59.972
If this is for a romantic picnic,
may I suggest this lavender one?

05:00.056 --> 05:05.228
No, it's not a romantic picnic,
but it is a special occasion.

05:13.611 --> 05:16.572
IROH: The moonflower
likes partial shade.

05:24.163 --> 05:25.456
( CHILD CRYING )

05:25.540 --> 05:27.750
WOMAN: It's okay, Shh, shh, shh.

05:27.834 --> 05:29.877
WOMAN: It's okay, Shh.

05:31.170 --> 05:33.631
( MUSIC PLAYING )

05:34.382 --> 05:37.510
♪ Leaves from the vine

05:37.635 --> 05:40.137
♪ Falling so slow

05:40.263 --> 05:47.103
♪ Like fragile, tiny shells
drifting in the foam

05:47.478 --> 05:53.734
♪ Little soldier boy,
come marching home

05:54.110 --> 05:57.154
♪ Brave soldier boy

05:59.657 --> 06:03.244
♪ Comes marching home ♪

06:05.621 --> 06:06.956
Yeowch!

06:07.039 --> 06:08.332
( LAUGHING )

06:24.599 --> 06:26.225
MAN: Hey!

06:26.309 --> 06:29.645
IROH: It is usually best to
admit mistakes when they occur.

06:30.021 --> 06:32.148
And to seek to restore honor.

06:32.231 --> 06:34.150
( STOMPING )

06:34.233 --> 06:38.905
When I'm through with you kids, the window
won't be the only thing that's broken!

06:39.030 --> 06:40.489
But not this time.

06:40.573 --> 06:41.657
Run!

06:49.624 --> 06:50.875
THIEF: You.

06:51.000 --> 06:52.710
Give me all your money!

06:56.047 --> 06:57.673
What are you doing?

06:57.757 --> 06:58.966
I'm mugging you!

06:59.050 --> 07:00.426
With that stance?

07:00.509 --> 07:01.636
Wha-?

07:01.719 --> 07:03.095
What are you talking about?

07:03.179 --> 07:04.805
Just give me your money,
old man!

07:05.181 --> 07:10.227
With a poor stance, you are unbalanced,
and you can be easily knocked over.

07:12.480 --> 07:13.481
Ugh!

07:18.736 --> 07:23.532
With a solid stance, you are
a much more serious threat.

07:27.370 --> 07:28.621
Much better!

07:28.996 --> 07:33.250
But to tell you the truth,
you do not look like the criminal type.

07:33.626 --> 07:35.294
I know, I'm...

07:35.628 --> 07:36.796
I'm just confused.

07:39.298 --> 07:41.801
THIEF: So you really think
I could be a good masseur?

07:41.884 --> 07:43.177
Of course!

07:44.845 --> 07:46.097
This is so great!

07:46.722 --> 07:48.265
No one has ever believed in me.

07:48.724 --> 07:52.061
While it is always best
to believe in oneself,

07:52.144 --> 07:56.148
a little help from others
can be a great blessing.

08:20.631 --> 08:22.800
IROH: Happy birthday, my son.

08:24.677 --> 08:27.471
If only I could have helped you.

08:28.806 --> 08:32.059
♪ Leaves from the vine

08:32.935 --> 08:35.438
♪ Falling so slow

08:35.521 --> 08:41.986
♪ Like fragile, tiny shells
drifting in the foam

08:42.570 --> 08:46.323
( CRYING ) ♪ Little soldier boy

08:46.407 --> 08:48.117
♪ Come marching home

08:49.201 --> 08:52.872
♪ Brave soldier boy

08:52.997 --> 08:56.584
♪ Comes marching home ♪

09:35.081 --> 09:36.207
Hey there, fella.

09:36.582 --> 09:37.666
AANG: You look hungry.

09:37.750 --> 09:38.751
Ahh!

09:42.338 --> 09:43.464
They are hungry.

09:45.883 --> 09:49.178
The Dai Li won't give me any money
because the kids stopped coming.

09:49.595 --> 09:52.681
And the kids won't come because
my zoo's nasty and broke.

09:53.265 --> 09:54.683
What kind of animal is that?

09:54.934 --> 09:56.227
Ooh, that's a rabbiroo.

09:56.310 --> 09:59.188
I wish I could get her a big,
open prairie, like she likes.

10:00.022 --> 10:01.774
I'd let her
hop her way to happiness.

10:04.026 --> 10:06.028
- Let's do it.
- Say again?

10:06.112 --> 10:09.031
There's a big open space right
outside the walls of the city.

10:09.115 --> 10:12.284
ZOOKEEPER: But how are you
gonna transport all these wild critters?

10:12.368 --> 10:14.370
Don't worry,
I'm great with animals.

10:22.920 --> 10:25.214
( SCREAMING )

10:32.805 --> 10:34.807
( SPUTTERING )

10:35.474 --> 10:37.101
My cab-

10:38.227 --> 10:39.812
Oh, forget it.

10:40.437 --> 10:42.898
( SCREAMING )

10:52.032 --> 10:54.243
This was so much easier
in my head.

10:59.248 --> 11:00.374
( INHALING )

11:15.097 --> 11:16.098
( CRYING )

11:23.105 --> 11:25.024
Oom-oom-oom, oom-oom-oom.

11:25.858 --> 11:27.568
But you have to open this gate!

11:27.651 --> 11:28.736
Or what?

11:28.819 --> 11:29.820
Or that!

11:33.574 --> 11:35.159
Open the gate!

12:10.194 --> 12:12.571
( GRUNTING )

12:21.413 --> 12:22.665
( LAUGHING )

12:30.297 --> 12:31.632
( SQUEAKING )

12:32.258 --> 12:35.302
Well, Mr. Zookeeper, how do you
like your new facilities?

12:35.386 --> 12:37.513
Excellent job, Avatar.

12:37.596 --> 12:40.266
You should think about working
with animals for a living.

12:40.349 --> 12:43.435
CHILD 1: Mommy, Miss Snowflake
got out of the house again.

12:43.519 --> 12:44.812
( HISSING )

12:44.895 --> 12:47.314
CHILD 2: Fluffikins, what are you
doing down there?

12:47.398 --> 12:48.983
( MEOWING )

12:49.066 --> 12:52.194
On second thought, you should
probably stick to saving people.

12:52.278 --> 12:54.530
( LAUGHING NERVOUSLY )

13:10.337 --> 13:12.256
( ANIMAL GRUNTING )

13:12.965 --> 13:14.383
( FAINT CONVERSATION )

13:15.384 --> 13:16.593
What's this?

13:16.677 --> 13:18.554
"Through all the long night,

13:18.637 --> 13:21.432
"Winter moon glows
with bright love.

13:21.515 --> 13:24.018
"Sleet, her silver tears."

13:24.476 --> 13:27.229
Ahh, poetry.

13:27.313 --> 13:28.856
( GRUNTING )

13:28.939 --> 13:30.149
Augh!

13:30.232 --> 13:31.233
( WOMEN GASPING )

13:32.735 --> 13:34.278
I am so sorry.

13:34.945 --> 13:36.739
Something struck me in the rear.

13:37.740 --> 13:41.118
I just... Wound up... Here?

13:41.493 --> 13:46.248
( LAUGHING )

13:48.459 --> 13:54.381
"Five, seven, then five syllables mark
a haiku, remarkable oaf."

13:57.384 --> 14:03.640
"They call me Sokka, that is,
in the water tribe. I am not an oaf."

14:03.807 --> 14:06.226
( LAUGHING )

14:06.477 --> 14:12.441
"Chittering monkey. In the spring he
climbs treetops and thinks himself tall."

14:12.900 --> 14:14.443
Ooh...

14:14.777 --> 14:19.782
"You think you're so smart, with your
fancy little words. This is not so hard."

14:20.240 --> 14:22.117
WOMEN: Ooh...

14:22.326 --> 14:27.623
"Whole seasons are spent mastering
the form, the style. None calls it easy."

14:27.706 --> 14:33.128
"I calls it easy. Like I paddle my canoe,
I'll paddle yours, too."

14:33.462 --> 14:36.840
( LAUGHING )

14:37.299 --> 14:40.010
"There's nuts and there's fruits.

14:40.094 --> 14:44.473
"In fall, the clean plum drops,
always to be squashed."

14:46.975 --> 14:49.311
"Squish-squash sling that slang,

14:49.395 --> 14:53.524
"I'm always right back at ya,
like my... Boomerang."

14:53.857 --> 14:56.485
( LAUGHING )

15:00.864 --> 15:04.535
"That's right, I'm Sokka,
it's pronounced with an 'Okka,

15:04.618 --> 15:07.496
"'young ladies, I rocked ya."

15:10.332 --> 15:11.333
( CRICKET CHIRPING )

15:15.712 --> 15:19.133
Uh, that's one too many
syllables there, bub.

15:22.594 --> 15:23.595
Augh!

15:26.807 --> 15:27.933
Poetry.

15:40.404 --> 15:42.573
Uncle, we have a problem.

15:43.699 --> 15:45.451
One of the customers
is on to us.

15:46.243 --> 15:49.413
Don't look now, but there is
a girl over there at the corner table.

15:49.496 --> 15:51.123
ZUKO: She knows we're Fire Nation.

15:51.999 --> 15:53.667
Didn't I say don't look?

15:54.126 --> 15:55.544
IROH: You're right, Zuko.

15:55.627 --> 15:58.088
I've seen that girl in here quite a lot.

15:58.547 --> 16:02.092
Seems to me she has
quite a little crush on you.

16:02.176 --> 16:03.177
What?

16:03.260 --> 16:04.761
Thank you for the tea.

16:06.597 --> 16:07.806
What's your name?

16:08.307 --> 16:09.600
My name's Lee.

16:09.683 --> 16:11.185
My uncle and I just moved here.

16:11.602 --> 16:14.104
Hi, Lee, my name's Jin.

16:14.188 --> 16:16.106
Thank you, and, well,

16:16.690 --> 16:19.985
I was wondering if you would
like to go out some time.

16:20.068 --> 16:21.278
He'd love to.

16:21.653 --> 16:24.323
Great! I'll meet you
in front of the shop at sundown.

16:37.377 --> 16:38.504
Hey.

16:38.587 --> 16:40.088
Well, look at you.

16:40.422 --> 16:41.798
You look so cute.

16:42.257 --> 16:45.219
It took my uncle
ten minutes to do my hair.

16:50.057 --> 16:52.684
So, how do you
like the city so far?

16:52.768 --> 16:53.977
It's okay.

16:54.394 --> 16:55.979
What do you like to do for fun?

16:56.063 --> 16:57.356
Nothing.

16:57.439 --> 17:00.400
Excuse me, sir, would you
and your girlfriend care for dessert?

17:00.484 --> 17:02.277
( SCREAMING ) She is not my girlfriend!

17:08.200 --> 17:12.204
You have...
Quite an appetite for a girl.

17:12.579 --> 17:14.373
Um, thanks?

17:15.832 --> 17:20.295
So, Lee, where were you and your uncle
living before you came here?

17:20.420 --> 17:25.259
( HESITATING ) Um, well, we've been
traveling around for a long time.

17:25.342 --> 17:27.928
Oh! Why were you traveling so much?

17:28.011 --> 17:31.473
We were, uh, part of this
traveling circus.

17:31.557 --> 17:32.724
Really?

17:32.808 --> 17:34.893
What did you do?
Wait, let me guess.

17:35.769 --> 17:36.770
You juggled.

17:38.105 --> 17:39.606
Yes, I juggled.

17:39.690 --> 17:41.650
I've always wanted to
learn how to juggle.

17:41.733 --> 17:43.068
Can you show me something?

17:46.154 --> 17:47.447
Uh...

17:49.783 --> 17:51.118
Whoa, uh!

17:51.660 --> 17:53.453
I haven't practiced for a while.

17:53.537 --> 17:54.955
JIN: It's all right.

17:55.789 --> 17:59.376
Hey, I want to show you
one of my favorite places in the city.

18:00.627 --> 18:03.380
JIN: I'm so excited for you
to see the firelight fountain.

18:03.463 --> 18:05.090
The lamps make the water sparkle,

18:05.173 --> 18:08.135
and reflect in the pool
in the most beautiful way.

18:10.512 --> 18:11.722
I can't believe it!

18:11.805 --> 18:13.015
JIN: They aren't lit.

18:16.893 --> 18:17.894
Close your eyes.

18:17.978 --> 18:18.979
And don't peek.

18:37.080 --> 18:39.291
ZUKO: Okay, Now you can look.

18:39.750 --> 18:41.585
Oh, wow...

18:45.213 --> 18:46.298
What happened?

18:46.381 --> 18:47.633
How did they light?

18:47.716 --> 18:49.051
What did you...

18:59.936 --> 19:01.438
I brought you something.

19:01.772 --> 19:03.982
ZUKO: It's a coupon
for a free cup of tea.

19:04.399 --> 19:06.943
Lee, this is so sweet.

19:07.903 --> 19:09.738
Don't thank me,
it was my uncle's idea.

19:09.821 --> 19:11.907
He thinks you're our
most valuable customer.

19:11.990 --> 19:13.617
Your uncle is a good teacher.

19:15.369 --> 19:17.496
I have something for you, too.

19:17.579 --> 19:19.998
Now it's your turn
to close your eyes.

19:27.798 --> 19:28.840
JIN: What's wrong?

19:29.341 --> 19:30.509
It's complicated.

19:30.592 --> 19:31.593
I have to go.

19:43.730 --> 19:45.565
How was your night, Prince Zuko?

19:50.654 --> 19:51.655
It was nice.

20:03.500 --> 20:05.085
( APPA GROWLING )

20:06.670 --> 20:07.963
( MOMO CHIRPING )

20:20.559 --> 20:22.310
( THUNDER CRASHING )

20:22.936 --> 20:24.271
( CHIRPING )

20:36.158 --> 20:37.576
( ROARING )

20:51.715 --> 20:53.467
( CHIRPING SADLY )

21:02.893 --> 21:04.144
( CHIRPING SADLY )

21:15.697 --> 21:16.948
( GROWLING )

21:19.201 --> 21:20.786
( SNARLING )

21:25.916 --> 21:28.752
( MEOWING AND SNARLING )

21:56.488 --> 21:59.407
( APPLAUSE )

22:05.914 --> 22:07.874
( GROWLING AND SNARLING )

22:17.968 --> 22:19.511
( GROWLING )

22:19.594 --> 22:20.679
( ROARING )

22:37.487 --> 22:40.198
( SPEAKING IN GIBBERISH )

22:41.825 --> 22:46.204
( SPEAKING IN GIBBERISH )

22:46.329 --> 22:49.749
( SNARLING AND MEOWING )

23:11.313 --> 23:12.856
( PURRING AND CHIRPING )

23:16.401 --> 23:17.402
( CHIRPING )

23:36.212 --> 23:38.965
( RAIN FALLING )
